# Verification

```bash
pipenv run python tests/verify.py
```

Exits non-zero on failure. Run it after touching `server/engine.py`. It checks
both hard invariants (tile independence, scale invariance) plus zoom fidelity,
colour pass-through, luminance response, edge bias, the smooth-area guard,
16-bit PNG validity, and each stage that ships at 0 (global grain, edge
softening/sanding, scatter, sharpening, film texture).

Stages that ship at 0 get their **own** checks that re-run tile independence
with the stage switched on — the default-parameter checks render straight past
them, so a kernel missing from `pad_for` would seam only there.

`ENGINE.render_view` / `render_crop` are no longer called by `main.py` but are
the **only** place the crop/zoom invariants are checked. Do not delete them.

## Trap when adding a check

`sanitize(None)` fills in **defaults, not zeros**. An override dict must zero
every *other* stage that could contribute to the same measurement — e.g. the
sanding check failed first time because `edge_jitter` defaults to 0.3 and was
adding its own wander. Zero unrelated amounts explicitly.

Note: `verify.py` has ~67 static `check()` call sites; the "79 checks" figure in
`CLAUDE.md`/`README.md` counts loop iterations, so the printed total is higher.
